The Workflow for Permanent Storage
To build this, you follow these three steps:
 
1. Create a "File Search Store"
Think of this as your permanent folder in the Gemini cloud.
 
Persistence: It stays forever until you manually delete it.
 
Capacity: You can store thousands of documents here.
 
2. Upload and Import Your Files
You upload your large files (PDF, JSON, TXT, etc.) and "import" them into that store.
 
Gemini will automatically chunk your large files (break them into small pieces) and index them.
 
While the original raw file you uploaded expires in 48 hours, the indexed version in the Store remains permanent.
 
3. Connect the Store to Zoho Desk (Deluge)
When a ticket comes in, your Deluge script tells Gemini: "Look at the ticket, then search my specific File Search Store to find the right category."

=============================================================================================================================================================

// Use your permanent Store ID here
storeId = "fileSearchStores/YOUR_STORE_ID";
 
payload = {
    "contents": [{
        "parts": [{"text": "Identify category and sub-category for this ticket: " + subject}]
    }],
    "tools": [{
        "file_search": {
            "file_search_store_names": [storeId]
        }
    }]
};
 
// Send to Gemini...

=============================================================================================================================================================

1. Create the File Search Store
This creates the "permanent container" for your files.
 
Method: POST
 
URL: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/fileSearchStores?key=YOUR_API_KEY
 
Headers: Content-Type: application/json
 
Body (raw JSON):
 
JSON
 
{
  "displayName": "Organization-Ticketing-KB"
}
The Response: You will receive a JSON object. Copy the "name" value (it looks like fileSearchStores/abc-123). This is your unique Store ID.
 
2. Upload and Index Your Large File
To add your file to this store permanently, you use the uploadToFileSearchStore endpoint. This is a multi-part upload.
 
Method: POST
 
URL: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/upload/v1beta/fileSearchStores/YOUR_STORE_ID:uploadToFileSearchStore?key=YOUR_API_KEY
 
Note: Replace YOUR_STORE_ID with the name you got in step 1 (e.g., fileSearchStores/abc-123).
 
Body: Select form-data.
 
Add a key named file.
 
Change the type from Text to File.
 
Select your large organization file from your computer.
 
Gemini will now start "chunking" and "embedding" your file. This takes a few seconds to a few minutes depending on the file size.
 
3. Verify the Content (Optional)
You can check if your file is successfully indexed and stored by listing the documents in your store.
 
Method: GET
 
URL: https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/fileSearchStores/YOUR_STORE_ID/documents?key=YOUR_API_KEY
 
4. Summary of Zoho Desk Integration
Once the store is set up in Postman, your Zoho Deluge script only needs to know that Store ID. You don't need to upload the file again.
 
In your Zoho script, your tools section in the API payload will look like this:
 
Code snippet
"tools": [
    {
        "file_search": {
            "file_search_store_names": ["fileSearchStores/your-actual-id-here"]
        }
    }
]
 
 
Why Postman is a good choice here:
Permanent: Unlike the temporary File API, the data you put into a fileSearchStore does not expire after 48 hours.
 
Scalable: You can add more files to the same store later by repeating Step 2.
 
No Code Setup: You handle the "Knowledge Base" setup visually in Postman and only use the ID in your ticketing app code.

